§6+====+

§8A talking turtle named Toortle visited the tavern and handed me their resume hoping to get a job. I couldn’t say no, I mean.... a talking turtle! So now (§opart-time§0§8) they work

#- §8behind the bar, looking pretty and selling our #1 Beet Beer (§oor should I say, drinking it instead and wrongly labelling it as '§7melk§8'§o, 
I don’t think they are going to last very long).

§0§8In other news, people are still acting strangely, telling me that I'm not safe!
#- §8A load of rubbish in my opinion. Although, a fellow traveller named R3d arrived in my office with a cursed hood stuck on their head screaming “§5WHEN ARE YOU GOING TO EXPLAIN ɨȶ?§8” I had no idea what they were talking about. They claimed someone, or something called ‘§5ɨȶ§8’ put the hood on them, 
#- §8but I’d never heard of ‘§5ɨȶ§8’ before and never seen such powerful magic either. 

So§6m§8e§6th§8in§6g.. 
            fe§8el§6s... 
                  §8wr§6ong… 

     §5ₒh nₒ yₒᵤ dₒn't!

§8but§8§8 that's none of my business.
             ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 
#- §6╔═.✵.════════╗
      §5The Library!
§6╚════════.✵.═╝
§8As I mentioned earlier, books are important! In fact, books are one of Craftadia’s only sources of entertainment. Craftadian’s indulge in the rich history of knowledge these books contain about the land they inhabit  
#- §8and journey adventurous escapes into brand new worlds. Books have been a part of this world for over a millennium. So it saddens me to say these days, books are a bit of a taboo subject. Specifically in the reading of them. 
Even more specifically ...§olecterns! 
#- §8A lectern is a reading desk with a slanted top, on which documents or books are placed as support for reading aloud, the problem is for quite a few months now, the books in Craftadia, just… §odon’t want to be read.§0§8 
Not out loud that is. Writers like myself can still write, publish and  
#- §8sell our books but whenever they are placed on a lectern they refuse to be opened, and the lectern itself cannot be moved or removed. This is a very strange phenomenon and highly confusing. 
Some outside sources (mainly the institutions known as §2§3§2[§§ADMIN] §8and §3[MOD]§8) have claimed
#- §8dark magic is involved. Something or someone does not want us to read books out loud or access them for free. Personally, this has affected me greatly because my library has vanished. I had a whole room filled with so much information and important historical records. §lAncient!  
#- §8Even my diary was in there, full of spells and notes from ever since I was born. It's a disaster! I’m sure other people are having the same difficulties, I have a friend who lost their library too, but I can’t help feeling this has something to do with §lmy library §0§8in particular, like...
#- §8this magazine for example... 

The way the book §6calls to me, §8and the touch… is that a… §6heartbeat?

§8§6Maybe I should… §8no I shouldn’t mention this. 

Someone else will figure this out 
I’m sure...  
#- §8This is not my problem!

I’m here to write, tend to the tavern, and live out my witchy life in peace, nothing more. 

§7-------------------
If §8ʏօʊ §7have been affected by this issue please email me at:
§8§nwitchmag@illegible.com

