§1How do I interpret the programmed actions?

§3⏺ §1To be able to understand the behaviour of your installation when the schedule timer is enabled, it is important to look at all programmed action of
#- §1yesterday. If the first programmed action for today is not active yet, the current status of your installation depends, most probably, but not necessarily, on the last programmed action from yesterday. 
§7(read the important note below)
#- §3⏺ §1If the first programmed action for today is already active, the current status of your installation depends, most probably, but not necessarily, on the parameters programmed in the first programmed action for today.
§7(read the important 
note below)
#- §3IMPORTANT NOTE BELOW
§8-------------------
§3✍ Note: §1To keep the operation of your installation simple, the schedule timer settings can be overruled by altering the current setting. 

§7("last command" overrules previous command until next scheduled command)
#- §3Conclusion:
§8-------------------
§3⏺ §1Although §2☑ §1is displayed somebody might have altered the settings. The next programmed action will overrule the altered settings and all settings return as programmed.

§7(do not play 
while sleeping)
